# Build-time env baked into the frontend web bundle for the hermetic e2e stack
# (dotenv-webpack reads it as apps/frontend/.env.prod; see stack.Dockerfile).
#
# REACT_APP_CLOUD_URL is the API path prefix nginx proxies to the backend — the
# same value the published images are built with.
#
# REACT_APP_VOICE_FILL_SCRIPTED allows Voice Fill's scripted speech and
# extractor models, so its flow can be driven with no model downloaded and no
# microphone. It only allows them: a page still has to be opened with
# `?voiceFill=scripted` to get them, so every journey that does not ask sees the
# app as a published image shows it. The published images are built from an env
# file the publish workflow writes itself, which never carries this key.
#
# A page that does not ask runs the real models, as production does: the real
# speech model alone, until there is a real extraction model. In a browser that
# can run Voice Fill (see the last paragraph) that page downloads Moonshine
# Small Streaming, 165 MB, from the Moonshine CDN the first time it is opened,
# shows the settings card with the speech dropdown alone, and offers the button
# once the model is ready; a Ramble is heard live, and "Done talking" ends in
# "Voice fill hit a problem". In a browser that cannot — a headless one with no
# WebGPU adapter — nothing of Voice Fill shows and nothing is downloaded.
#
# A scripted run also lists the real speech model, Moonshine Small Streaming,
# after the scripted ones. Nothing of it is fetched unless it is picked on the
# settings card; picked, its files are downloaded from the Moonshine CDN and
# the Ramble is heard through the microphone, with the scripted extractor still
# reading it. A browser started with a fake audio capture
# (`--use-fake-device-for-media-stream --use-file-for-fake-audio-capture=<wav>`)
# can be driven through that with no one speaking.
#
# A scripted run also lists the real extraction model, Gemma 4 E2B, after the
# scripted ones. Nothing of it is fetched unless it is picked on the settings
# card; picked, its file (2 GB) is downloaded from Hugging Face and the scripted
# Ramble is read by the real model, which needs a WebGPU adapter to load.
#
# A scripted run still checks the phone as a real one would be (a microphone
# API, a WebGPU adapter, a cross-origin isolated page) and shows nothing of
# Voice Fill where one is missing. A journey in a browser with no WebGPU adapter
# adds `&voiceFillPhone=capable` to be walked through all the same.
REACT_APP_CLOUD_URL=/api/
REACT_APP_VOICE_FILL_SCRIPTED=true
